-- s 187(3) binds only for a request made within 30 days after the costs became payable (s 187(2)): costs payable on
-- 1 May 2029, a request on 1 June 2029 is late and gets no date; one on 31 May gets 21 June 2029. A small proprietary
-- company is not a commercial or government client and has the right.
#ASSERT `By what date must I be given the itemised bill` `as the client` `a lump sum bill` `an individual` (Date 1 5 2029) (Date 1 6 2029) EQUALS `no date: the law practice need not give it, as the request was made more than 30 days after the costs became payable (s 187(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `By what date must I be given the itemised bill` `as the client` `a lump sum bill` `an individual` (Date 1 5 2029) (Date 31 5 2029) EQUALS `by` (Date 21 6 2029)
#ASSERT `Can I still ask for an itemised bill` `as the client` `a lump sum bill` `a small proprietary company or other client` (Date 1 5 2029) (Date 31 5 2029) EQUALS yes
-- r 15(3): a summary conviction under transport or traffic legislation about parking is never prescribed, even with a
-- licence disqualification; one about neither parking nor driving, or not under that legislation, always is.
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board` `as the lawyer` TRUE `I was convicted of an offence` `a summary offence` `a transport or traffic offence about parking` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `on reporting` `no: neither s 51 nor s 88 requires it`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board` `as the lawyer` TRUE `I was convicted of an offence` `a summary offence` `a transport or traffic offence about neither parking nor driving or operating a vehicle` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `on reporting` `yes: notify the Board in writing within 7 days (s 51(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board` `as the lawyer` TRUE `I was convicted of an offence` `a summary offence` `not an offence under transport or traffic legislation` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `on reporting` `yes: notify the Board in writing within 7 days (s 51(1))`
#ASSERT `Must I report this to the Legal Practice Board` `as the lawyer` TRUE `I was convicted of an offence` `a summary offence` `a transport or traffic offence about parking` FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `on reporting` (`Must I report this to the Board` `I was convicted of an offence` (`The offence` WITH `class` IS `a summary offence`, `under transport or traffic legislation` IS TRUE, `about parking` IS TRUE, `about driving or operating a vehicle` IS TRUE, `I was sentenced to imprisonment` IS FALSE, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS 0, `licence disqualification ordered` IS TRUE, `drink or drug driving under the NSW or Victorian Act` IS FALSE))
-- s 129(2)(d): money for investment received at the client's direction and invested in the ordinary course is trust
-- money, so it goes into the general trust account; if not, it is not trust money.
#ASSERT `Where must my firm put the money` `as the lawyer` TRUE `money for investment purposes` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the money goes` `into the general trust account as soon as practicable, held only for the client and paid out only on the client's direction (ss 137, 138)`
#ASSERT `Where must my law practice put my money` `as the client` TRUE `money for investment purposes` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the money goes` `not trust money: the trust money provisions do not govern it`
